.TH CBMAP_GET_ELEM_COPY 3 "2026-09-13" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cbmap_get_elem_copy \- copy the value associated with a key out of a BST map
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cbstmap.h>

ccol_retval_t cbmap_get_elem_copy(cbmap cbm, const cmap_pair *key_pair,
                                  void *target_buf, size_t target_buf_size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Searches the map for key_pair and copies the associated value into
target_buf. The buffer size must match the stored value's size exactly;
a partial copy is never performed, so a value can never be silently
truncated. This is stricter than chmap_get_elem_copy(3), which copies
min(value_size, target_buf_size) bytes instead.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cbm              BST map to search
key_pair         Key to look up
target_buf       Buffer to receive the value copy
target_buf_size  Size of target_buf, which must equal the stored value's
                 own size
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success        - Key found, value copied into target_buf
ccol_key_not_found  - Key does not exist in map
ccol_invalid_args   - target_buf_size does not match the stored value's
                      size, or key_pair's size does not match a
                      fixed-width key type's own size (see
                      cbmap_create_full(3))
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(log n) complexity
Requires an exact value size match, unlike chmap_get_elem_copy(3)
target_buf is left untouched on every failure
Asserts if cbm is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cbmap_get_elem_ref (3),
.BR cbmap_insert_elem (3),
.BR cbmap_create_full (3)
